{
  "info": {
    "name": "Server Rules Service",
    "schema": "https://schema.getpostman.com/json/collection/v2.1.0/collection.json",
    "description": "Server Rules Service, tested through the Gateway (http://localhost:8090). Its own ports are not published, so the Gateway is the only way in.\n\nSELF-CONTAINED: folder 0 registers and logs in a throwaway player (a fresh one every run). Run the collection top to bottom with the Collection Runner.\n\nNOTE: Replace Rules wipes the previous rule set. This collection leaves the rule set it last wrote ('Only FAF students', plus the second rule from the multi-rule test) in the database.\n\nWHAT IT PROVES\n- Folder 1: the Gateway enforces the token (401).\n- Folder 2: GET/PUT /rules, persistence, replace semantics, validation (422/400).\n- Folder 3 (Lab 3, grades 4-5): two replicas behind the Gateway; round-robin alternates them; a rule written through one replica is read through the other (instance-agnostic).\n\nREQUIRES the service to answer with an X-Instance-Id header (the container id). Folder 3 fails without it.\n\nNOT COVERED HERE\n- GET /health: polled by Service Discovery inside the Compose network, not routed by the Gateway. Check it with: docker compose logs discovery-service\n- gRPC EvaluateApplicant (used by Moderation Service): not reachable from Postman because the port is not published.\n- Circuit breaker: this service makes no outgoing calls, so it has none (the lab asks for it only in services that make calls).\n"
  },
  "item": [
    {
      "name": "0. Setup (Player Service, through the Gateway)",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "Register tester",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "prerequest",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.collectionVariables.set('run_id', String(Date.now()));"
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('201 Created', () => pm.response.to.have.status(201));"
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Content-Type",
                "value": "application/json"
              }
            ],
            "auth": {
              "type": "noauth"
            },
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"username\": \"srtest{{run_id}}\",\n  \"email\": \"srtest{{run_id}}@example.com\",\n  \"password\": \"secret123\"\n}",
              "options": {
                "raw": {
                  "language": "json"
                }
              }
            },
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{base_url}}/players",
              "host": [
                "{{base_url}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "players"
              ]
            }
          },
          "response": []
        },
        {
          "name": "Login tester",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "function decode(t){ try { return JSON.parse(atob(t.split('.')[1].replace(/-/g,'+').replace(/_/g,'/'))); } catch(e){ return null; } }",
                  "",
                  "pm.test('200 OK', () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));",
                  "const token = pm.response.json().token;",
                  "pm.test('a JWT came back', () => pm.expect(token).to.be.a('string').and.not.be.empty);",
                  "pm.collectionVariables.set('token', token);",
                  "const claims = decode(token);",
                  "if (claims) pm.collectionVariables.set('player_id', claims.sub);"
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Content-Type",
                "value": "application/json"
              }
            ],
            "auth": {
              "type": "noauth"
            },
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"email\": \"srtest{{run_id}}@example.com\",\n  \"password\": \"secret123\"\n}",
              "options": {
                "raw": {
                  "language": "json"
                }
              }
            },
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{base_url}}/players/login",
              "host": [
                "{{base_url}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "players",
                "login"
              ]
            }
          },
          "response": []
        }
      ]
    },
